rem signed-slice `index` sign-extension fixture (i8/i16/i32/i64) — a negative
rem element must come back NEGATIVE on BOTH backends. A both-agree-wrong bug was
rem here: `index` read the raw bytes UNSIGNED, so slice i32 of -1 → 4294967295.
rem The element's TYPE is signed, so index must sign-extend. Unsigned stays unsigned.
module m .

fn s8  output i64 . input s slice i8  . do return widen i64 (index s 0) . end .
fn s16 output i64 . input s slice i16 . do return widen i64 (index s 0) . end .
fn s32 output i64 . input s slice i32 . do return widen i64 (index s 0) . end .
fn s64 output i64 . input s slice i64 . do return widen i64 (index s 0) . end .

rem positive control — a small positive signed element stays positive.
fn s32p output i64 . input s slice i32 . do return widen i64 (index s 0) . end .

rem unsigned control — index of 0xFFFFFFFF stays 4294967295, NOT -1.
fn u32 output i64 . input s slice u32 . do return widen i64 (index s 0) . end .

rem view_array route — a signed typed view must sign-extend too.
type bytes slice u8 .
fn v32 output i64 . input b bytes . do return widen i64 (index (view_array i32 b) 0) . end .
